---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { readSettings, buildCanonicalUrl } from "../utils/settings";

const settings = readSettings();
const canonical = buildCanonicalUrl(settings, { path: "/privacy" });
---
<Base
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How we handle your data."
  canon={canonical}
>
  <article class="prose prose-neutral max-w-none">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p><em>Last reviewed: July 12, 2026</em></p>
    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>
      WitchClick is mostly static. Its configured Plausible analytics records aggregate page views and interaction events without
      using analytics cookies. Affiliate clicks may be counted as events, but WitchClick no longer keeps a local history of the
      full destinations you visit. We do not sell personal data.
    </p>
    <h2>Information kept on your device</h2>
    <p>
      Comfort preferences and any local ritual-shelf notes use your browser’s local storage. They stay on that device unless you
      clear the site’s storage. They are not an authenticated account or cloud backup.
    </p>
    <h2>Fonts, forms, and external links</h2>
    <p>
      Pages request font files from Google Fonts, which receives standard connection data such as your IP address. Forms only
      submit when a delivery endpoint is configured and show an unavailable message otherwise. Affiliate and partner links send
      you to an external retailer or organization; that destination applies its own privacy policy and may use tracking parameters.
    </p>
    <h2>Cookies and advertising</h2>
    <p>
      WitchClick does not currently use an analytics-cookie consent control because its configured analytics is cookieless. If
      advertising or another cookie-setting service is enabled later, this policy and the site’s consent controls must be updated
      before that service loads.
    </p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>For privacy questions, contact <a href="mailto:streamthreadsystems@gmail.com">streamthreadsystems@gmail.com</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
